<title>USA: Schenectady, NY seeks tax rise to close budget gap.</title>
<headline>Schenectady, NY seeks tax rise to close budget gap.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The mayor of Schenectady and eight of his department heads spent $800 of their own money to pay for a newspaper advertisement calling for the City Council to approve an 11.5 percent tax rise to close a budget gap.</p>
<p>Mayor Al Jurczynski said that raising taxes was the only way that the town would be able to afford to continue to provide many services.</p>
<p>The council faces a deadline of midnight Thursday.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
